@biohub makes a major investment in an open data foundation for AI-accelerated biology. We at @arcinstitute are excited to be part of this effort through our existing and future partnerships with Biohub. Biological models need an ocean of high-quality data to explore.

Today we’re launching the Virtual Biology Initiative to generate the data to unlock scaling laws in biology and build accurate predictive models of the cell. Digital representations of proteins are already expanding our understanding of life at the molecular level and accelerating the design of molecules and medicines. Accurate digital representations of the cell could reveal the mechanisms responsible for disease and show how to reverse them.

Biohub is contributing to this effort as both a funder and a builder, committing $100M over the next five years to support work beyond Biohub. The data generated will be available to the worldwide scientific community, and we invite other scientific teams and funders to join.

@alexrives: "Scaling laws are powering AI. It’s time to scale biology. The cell is orders of magnitude more complex, and we will need to create the data in just a few years rather than decades."
